# Line endings are normalised on the way in, so a file written on Windows or by
# a tool defaulting to CRLF lands in the repository as LF like everything else.
#
# Eight culture branches arrived carrying 121 CRLF findings between them. The
# canon validator catches them, but only after a push and a CI round, and
# `prettier` did not: its `endOfLine` was "auto", which preserves whatever it
# finds rather than deciding. Both halves are fixed - this normalises on commit,
# and prettier now writes LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
